Examples 4 and 5 show a pattern for \(\lim_{x\to\pm\infty}\) of (polynomial)/(polynomial). Compare the degrees (highest powers):
1. degree of numerator < degree of denominator: limit 0 (Example 5);
2. degrees equal: limit = ratio of the leading coefficients, e.g. \(\lim_{x\to\infty}\frac{3x^{2}+1}{x^{2}-5} = 3\);
3. degree of numerator > degree of denominator: the fraction grows without bound, limit \(+\infty\) or \(-\infty\) (Example 4).
Use this only to check your answer; in the exam show the division.
